IMPORT prelude

-- Societies Act 1966 (Singapore) -- powers of entry, search and investigation; prosecution,
-- composition and jurisdiction; service; and the rules about a registered society's property, suits,
-- dissolution and officers' liability: ss 26 to 37.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 33A (amending the Schedule), s 34(1) (the regulation-making power: no regulation was
-- retrieved), s 38 (transitional).

§ `Societies Act 1966 -- ss 26 to 37`

§§ `26, 27, 28 -- entry, search and arrest`

-- s 26: "The Registrar or an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate or any police officer authorised in writing
-- by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate may AT ANY TIME enter any place which he has
-- REASON TO BELIEVE is kept or used by any REGISTERED society or any of its members as a place of meeting,
-- business or other activity of the society."
-- s 27: where the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate "has reason to believe that any
-- registered society is being used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order ... or
-- incompatible with the rules and objects", he may enter, or authorise a police officer to enter, "with or
-- without assistance and USING FORCE for that purpose, if necessary", and "may search ... that place and
-- ANY PERSON found in or escaping from that place for evidence".
-- s 28(1): "Any Magistrate or Justice of the Peace or POLICE OFFICER NOT BELOW THE RANK OF ASSISTANT
-- SUPERINTENDENT may enter ... using force in either case, if necessary, any dwelling house or other
-- building, or any place in which he has reasonable ground to believe that a meeting of an UNLAWFUL society
-- ... is being held, or that any books, accounts, writings, banners or insignia ... are concealed ..., and
-- to ARREST ... ALL PERSONS FOUND IN THE HOUSE and to search that house, building or place, and seize ...
-- all books, accounts, writings, banners, documents, flags, insignia, arms and other articles".
-- s 28(2): arrested persons and seized articles "may be detained in custody till they can conveniently be
-- brought before a District Court or Magistrate's Court".
--
-- NO WARRANT IS REQUIRED by ss 26 and 27 and none is mentioned. s 26 is subject only to "reason to believe"
-- and applies to every registered society and every place it uses, including a member's home. s 27's
-- search extends to a person "found in or escaping from" the place. And s 28 lets those who enter arrest
-- everyone present, not only those reasonably suspected, and detain them "till they can conveniently" be
-- brought before a court, with no time stated.
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Registrar`
    `an Assistant Registrar`
    `a Magistrate`
    `a Justice of the Peace`
    `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`
    `a police officer below that rank authorised in writing by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate`
    `a police officer below that rank with no authorisation`
    `anyone else`

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Assistant Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer below that rank authorised in writing by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 27's power is given to the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate, who may authorise a
-- police officer; a police officer acts only on that authority.
GIVEN `the person` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may enter and search under section 27` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Assistant Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer below that rank authorised in writing by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 28 is wider about WHO: a Justice of the Peace, and a police officer of the rank of assistant
-- superintendent or above acting on their own motion.
GIVEN `the person` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Justice of the Peace` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer below that rank authorised in writing by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 26 and 27 require a warrant` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 28 confines the arrest to persons reasonably suspected of involvement` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 28 states a time within which an arrested person must be brought before a court` IF
    FALSE

§§ `29, 29A, 29B -- investigation`

-- s 29: the powers may be used (a) to investigate a registered society's operations for compliance, including
-- whether an offence has been committed; (b) to investigate the existence or operations of any unlawful or
-- suspected unlawful society; (c) to determine whether information provided to the Registrar is correct.
-- s 29A(1): the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar may (a) where he reasonably believes a person has
-- committed an offence, require evidence of identity; (b) require any person whom he reasonably believes has
-- any information, document or article he reasonably requires for a s 29 purpose to provide it and explain
-- it within a reasonable period; (c) issue a written notice requiring any person within Singapore who
-- appears to be acquainted with the facts to attend; (d) examine orally any such person, before or after
-- anyone is charged.
-- s 29A(2): if satisfied after due inquiry that a person examined "is a MEMBER OF AN UNLAWFUL SOCIETY or has
-- REFUSED to give information or has given FALSE information as to the existence or operations of an unlawful
-- society or suspected unlawful society", he may order "a PHOTOGRAPH AND FINGER IMPRESSIONS" to be taken.
-- s 29A(4): a person examined "is bound to state truly what the person knows ..., EXCEPT that the person need
-- not say anything that might expose the person to a CRIMINAL CHARGE, PENALTY OR FORFEITURE".
-- s 29A(6): on non-compliance with the written notice, the Registrar may report to a Magistrate who may issue
-- a warrant ordering compliance.
-- s 29B(1): failing without reasonable excuse to do what is required: a fine not exceeding $10,000.
-- s 29B(2) and (3): intentionally altering, suppressing or destroying what was required, or making a false or
-- misleading statement: $10,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 29B(4): a defence, to be proved on a balance of probabilities, that the accused (a) does not possess the
-- thing, or (b) took all reasonable steps to obtain it and was unable to.
-- s 29B(5): "it is a reasonable excuse ... to refuse or fail to provide any information, produce any document or
-- article or answer any question if doing so might TEND TO INCRIMINATE that person."
--
-- The privilege is carried twice, in different words: s 29A(4) protects what might expose the person to a
-- criminal charge, penalty or forfeiture, and s 29B(5) protects what might tend to incriminate. It does not
-- protect a false answer: s 29B(2) has no such excuse. And it protects against compelled self-incrimination only;
-- a person who has been photographed and fingerprinted under s 29A(2) because they refused to answer has been
-- identified by the refusal.
DECLARE InvestigationFacts HAS
    `the purpose is one of the three in section 29` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the power is exercised by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar reasonably believes the person has the information or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable period was specified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person failed to provide or produce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `providing it might tend to incriminate the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person does not possess the information or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person took all reasonable steps to obtain it and could not` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN InvestigationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a requirement under section 29A(1)(b) is validly made` IF
        `the facts`'s `the purpose is one of the three in section 29`
    AND `the facts`'s `the power is exercised by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar`
    AND `the facts`'s `the Registrar reasonably believes the person has the information or thing`
    AND `the facts`'s `a reasonable period was specified`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN InvestigationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` IF
        `a requirement under section 29A(1)(b) is validly made` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `the person failed to provide or produce`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the person has a reasonable excuse`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `providing it might tend to incriminate the person`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the person does not possess the information or thing`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the person took all reasonable steps to obtain it and could not`

DECLARE ExaminationFacts HAS
    `satisfied after due inquiry that the person is a member of an unlawful society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfied that the person refused to give information about an unlawful or suspected unlawful society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfied that the person gave false information about an unlawful or suspected unlawful society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar considers it advisable to identify the person` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN ExaminationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may order a photograph and finger impressions` IF
        `the facts`'s `the Registrar considers it advisable to identify the person`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `satisfied after due inquiry that the person is a member of an unlawful society`
         OR  `the facts`'s `satisfied that the person refused to give information about an unlawful or suspected unlawful society`
         OR  `the facts`'s `satisfied that the person gave false information about an unlawful or suspected unlawful society`)

DECLARE AnswerFacts HAS
    `the answer would expose the person to a criminal charge, penalty or forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person gave a false answer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN AnswerFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is bound to answer under section 29A(4)` IF
    NOT `the answer`'s `the answer would expose the person to a criminal charge, penalty or forfeiture`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the privilege against self-incrimination excuses a false answer` IF
    FALSE

DECLARE FalseStatementFacts HAS
    `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed what was required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made a statement the person knows or ought reasonably to know is, or is reckless as to whether it is, false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A FalseStatementFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 29B(2)` IF
        `the facts`'s `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed what was required`
    OR  `the facts`'s `made a statement the person knows or ought reasonably to know is, or is reckless as to whether it is, false or misleading in a material particular`

§§ `30, 30A, 31, 32 -- charging, composing, trying and forfeiting`

-- s 30(1): "Except in the case of persons ARRESTED UNDER SECTION 28, no person shall be charged with an offence
-- under this Act ... unless the SANCTION IN WRITING of the Registrar or of an Assistant Registrar has been first
-- obtained."
-- s 30(2): with the Public Prosecutor's authorisation, prosecutions in a District Court or Magistrate's Court
-- may be conducted by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar, or a person they authorise.
--
-- Everyone arrested under s 28 can be charged without anyone's sanction; everyone else needs the Registrar's.
GIVEN `the person was arrested under section 28` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar sanctioned the charge in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be charged` IF
        `the person was arrested under section 28`
    OR  `the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar sanctioned the charge in writing`

-- s 30A(1): the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar "may compound any offence ... that is PRESCRIBED AS A
-- COMPOUNDABLE OFFENCE by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum NOT
-- EXCEEDING ONE HALF of the amount of the MAXIMUM FINE that is prescribed for the offence."
-- s 30A(2): on payment, no further proceedings. s 30A(3): the sum goes to the Consolidated Fund.
--
-- Half of the maximum fine, whatever the offence: for an offence punishable by a $10,000 fine OR imprisonment
-- OR both, the sum is capped by the fine alone.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the maximum fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the most that may be collected to compound the offence` IS
    IF   `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN JUST (`the maximum fine in dollars` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the compound sum has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further proceedings may be taken for the offence` IF
    NOT `the compound sum has been paid`

-- s 31(1): an offence under s 14(2) "may be tried by a District Court which may pass the sentence specified in
-- that section". s 31(2): every other offence "may be tried by a District Court or by a Magistrate's Court".
DECLARE OffenceKind IS ONE OF
    `an offence under section 14(2)`
    `any other offence under the Act or regulations`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN OffenceKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Magistrate's Court may try the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence under section 14(2)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 32: "Any books, accounts, writings, banners, insignia or other property belonging to any unlawful society
-- shall be forfeited and given to the Registrar or to an Assistant Registrar." Forfeiture follows from the
-- property belonging to the society; it does not wait for a conviction.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forfeiture under section 32 waits for a conviction` IF
    FALSE

§§ `33 -- serving documents`

-- s 33(3): a document for an individual may be served by (a) giving it personally; (b) prepaid registered post to
-- the specified address or, if none, the residential or business address; (c) leaving it with an adult
-- apparently resident or employed there; (d) AFFIXING A COPY in a conspicuous place at the residential or
-- business address; or (e) email to the last email address.
-- s 33(6): service by email takes effect "when the email becomes capable of being retrieved"; by registered post
-- "2 DAYS AFTER THE DAY the document was posted (even if it is returned undelivered)".
-- s 33(7): service by email "may be effected only with the person's PRIOR CONSENT (express or implied)".
-- s 33(2): the section does not apply to documents in court proceedings.
--
-- A notice to a person who has moved is served by affixing a copy to the old door, and by post even if it comes
-- back. The Gazette notification under s 6 is outside this section, which concerns documents "permitted or
-- required ... to be served on a person".
DECLARE ServiceMethod IS ONE OF
    `giving it to the individual personally`
    `prepaid registered post`
    `leaving it with an adult apparently resident or employed at the address`
    `affixing a copy in a conspicuous place at the address`
    `email, with the person's prior consent`
    `email, without the person's consent`
    `some other method`

GIVEN `the method` IS A ServiceMethod
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method is one section 33(3) allows` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `email, without the person's consent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `some other method` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the day the document was posted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day service by registered post takes effect` IS
    `the day the document was posted` PLUS 2

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `return of a posted document undelivered prevents service taking effect` IF
    FALSE

§§ `34(2) -- breach of regulations`

-- s 34(2): a regulation may provide that a breach is an offence with a fine "not exceeding $1,000 and, where the
-- breach is a continuing one, to a fine not exceeding $100 for every day after the first day during which the
-- breach continues."
`the maximum fine for a first breach of a regulation, in dollars` MEANS 1000
`the further daily fine for a continuing breach, in dollars` MEANS 100

GIVEN `the number of days the breach continued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most that may be imposed for a regulation breach` IS
    IF   `the number of days the breach continued` AT MOST 1
    THEN `the maximum fine for a first breach of a regulation, in dollars`
    ELSE `the maximum fine for a first breach of a regulation, in dollars`
             PLUS ((`the number of days the breach continued` MINUS 1) TIMES `the further daily fine for a continuing breach, in dollars`)

§§ `35 -- a registered society's property, suits, and dissolution`

-- s 35(1) applies to every registered society:
--   (a) movable property not vested in trustees is vested in the governing body, and may be described as
--       the governing body's;
--   (b) it may sue or be sued in the name in which it was registered;
--   (c) an originating claim may be served on an officer, or left at or posted to the registered address;
--   (d) "except as otherwise provided in section 36, NO JUDGMENT in any suit against a registered society
--       shall be put into force against the PERSON OR PROPERTY OF ANY OFFICER OR MEMBER of the society but
--       only against the PROPERTY OF THE SOCIETY";
--   (e) a member in arrears, or who detains or damages society property, may be sued by the society;
--   (f) a member who steals or embezzles society property is prosecutable as a non-member would be;
--   (g) "subject to subsection (2), IN THE ABSENCE OF ANY SPECIFIC PROVISION IN THE RULES of a society, any
--       number NOT LESS THAN THREE-FIFTHS of the members of the society FOR THE TIME BEING RESIDENT IN
--       SINGAPORE may determine that it shall be dissolved forthwith, or at a time agreed upon"; and
--   (h) "NO society shall be dissolved unless three-fifths of the members so resident ... have expressed a wish
--       for such dissolution by their votes delivered IN PERSON OR BY PROXY at a GENERAL MEETING convened for
--       the purpose."
-- s 35(2): "In the event of any dispute arising among the members of the governing body or the members of the
-- society, the adjustment of its affairs shall be referred to the General Division of the High Court".
--
-- (h) is unqualified. It makes a three-fifths vote of ALL resident members, not of those present or voting, a
-- condition of any dissolution, and it is not confined to a society whose rules are silent, which (g) is. A
-- rule that allowed dissolution by a smaller vote would conflict with (h). The vote must be cast at a general
-- meeting convened for the purpose, in person or by proxy.
DECLARE DissolutionVote HAS
    `members resident in Singapore for the time being` IS A NUMBER
    `of whom voted for dissolution in person or by proxy at a general meeting convened for the purpose` IS A NUMBER
    `the rules make a specific provision about dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rules require a smaller proportion than three-fifths` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the vote` IS A DissolutionVote
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `three-fifths of the resident members have voted for dissolution` IF
    (5 TIMES `the vote`'s `of whom voted for dissolution in person or by proxy at a general meeting convened for the purpose`)
        AT LEAST (3 TIMES `the vote`'s `members resident in Singapore for the time being`)

-- (h) is a condition of any dissolution: necessary, whatever the rules say.
GIVEN `the vote` IS A DissolutionVote
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society may be dissolved by its members` IF
    `three-fifths of the resident members have voted for dissolution` `the vote`

-- (g) is the default: where the rules are silent, the three-fifths vote suffices.
GIVEN `the vote` IS A DissolutionVote
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the default rule in section 35(1)(g) applies` IF
    NOT `the vote`'s `the rules make a specific provision about dissolution`

GIVEN `the vote` IS A DissolutionVote
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rule allowing dissolution by a smaller vote is effective` IF
    FALSE

-- s 35(1)(d) and s 36.
GIVEN `the judgment is against the society` IS A BOOLEAN, `section 36 applies to the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the judgment may be enforced against an officer or member personally` IF
        `the judgment is against the society`
    AND `section 36 applies to the officer`

§§ `36 -- security for costs, and officers' personal liability`

-- s 36(1): where a registered society or any of its officers purporting to act for it "is claimant in any action
-- or other legal proceeding", the court may, if it appears "by credible testimony that there is reason to
-- believe that the society or the officer will be UNABLE TO PAY THE COSTS of the defendant if successful",
-- require security and stay the proceedings until it is given.
-- s 36(2): "Where a society is REQUIRED to give security ... and the amount of the security is NOT SUFFICIENT to
-- pay the costs of the defendant -- (a) the officers of the society WHO APPROVED the institution of the action;
-- and (b) any person who, on SUBSEQUENTLY BECOMING an officer, does not take any REASONABLE MEASURE for the
-- purpose of seeking the discontinuance of the action, shall be JOINTLY AND SEVERALLY liable for any part of
-- the costs awarded against the society which, after deducting the amount of the security, REMAINS UNSATISFIED
-- AFTER ONE MONTH from the date the costs became payable."
--
-- This is the one exception to s 35(1)(d). The liability attaches only where security was REQUIRED and was
-- insufficient, and only to two classes: the officers who approved the suit, and any later officer who does not
-- try to stop it. An officer who did not approve it and was already in office is not liable. A later officer is
-- liable for the failure to try, so that taking office imposes a duty to look at the society's litigation.
DECLARE CostsFacts HAS
    `the society was claimant, or an officer purporting to act for it was` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court required security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the security given was not sufficient to pay the defendant's costs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person was an officer who approved the institution of the action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person became an officer later` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person took a reasonable measure to seek discontinuance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since the costs became payable` IS A NUMBER
    `part of the costs remains unsatisfied after deducting the security` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A CostsFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 36(2) applies to the society` IF
        `the facts`'s `the society was claimant, or an officer purporting to act for it was`
    AND `the facts`'s `the court required security`
    AND `the facts`'s `the security given was not sufficient to pay the defendant's costs`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A CostsFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` IF
        `section 36(2) applies to the society` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `part of the costs remains unsatisfied after deducting the security`
    AND `the facts`'s `months since the costs became payable` GREATER THAN 1
    AND (    `the facts`'s `this person was an officer who approved the institution of the action`
         OR  (    `the facts`'s `this person became an officer later`
              AND NOT `the facts`'s `this person took a reasonable measure to seek discontinuance`))

§§ `37 -- the power to exempt`

-- s 37: "The Minister may at his discretion in writing exempt any society REGISTERED UNDER THIS ACT from all or
-- any of the provisions of this Act."
--
-- The power is to exempt a REGISTERED society. It does not reach a society that is not registered, and so
-- cannot be the source of any exemption for an unregistered group from the unlawful-society offences in s 14;
-- that has to come from elsewhere. No exemption order was retrieved.
GIVEN `the society is registered under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister has exempted it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act's provisions are disapplied to the society by section 37` IF
        `the society is registered under the Act`
    AND `the Minister has exempted it in writing`

GIVEN `the society is registered under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 37 can exempt an unregistered society from section 14` IF
    FALSE
